{"description":"Make the control-plane connection survive network interruption without user intervention.\n\nExponential backoff with full jitter, capped — a fixed retry interval would make the whole fleet reconnect in lockstep every time the coordinator restarts. Application-level heartbeat with ping and pong, because a socket can remain open while the peer is gone. Session resumption by acknowledged position rather than a full re-handshake.\n\nThe connection state machine is explicit: disconnected, connecting, handshaking, online, degraded.","acceptanceCriteria":"1. Killing the coordinator and restarting it reconnects every client without user action.\n2. Retry intervals are jittered: twenty simulated clients reconnecting after a coordinator restart do not cluster into a single spike.\n3. A peer that stops responding while the socket stays open is detected by heartbeat within the configured dead-peer interval.\n4. Reconnect resumes from the acknowledged position instead of replaying the whole queue.\n5. All of the above is verified through the deterministic harness with injected loss, latency and partition — reproducibly, not by hand.\n6. The connection state is visible to the user at all times."}